// these graphs (named in `proof`). `area` is the three-character MSC class, as in data/concepts.js; the real division
// algebras (dimension 1, 2, 4, 8) are lie:bott-milnor-kervaire. `concepts` are ids of data/concepts.js or carry the prefix of another folder.
// `fromDefinitions: true` marks a theorem whose usual proof uses only definitions and axioms of its area and no
// theorem (it has no premises); a theorem without premises that rests on theory outside these graphs carries
// `foundation: true`, and its `proof` names that theory.
// References to theorems of other folders: "ca:", "ct:", "gt:", "ent:", "top:", "ana:", "ag:", "ant:", "ar:", "rt:";
